    content: "I have been meaning to start writing on this website for a while now, and today is the day! I thought it would be a great way to share my thoughts, experiences, and ideas with the world. So here we go \u2014 welcome to my blog!\n\n## A Little About Me\n\nMy name is Aufa Riduan Cahyadi. I'm passionate about **backend development**, **network infrastructure**, and **system automation**. Currently, I work in a university computer lab where I manage and maintain servers and lab facilities.\n\nOutside of work, I'm a dedicated **homelab enthusiast**. I spend my free time self-hosting applications, managing virtualized environments with Proxmox, deploying services via Docker, and configuring secure networks using WireGuard and Tailscale. There's something deeply satisfying about building your own infrastructure from scratch!\n\n## What to Expect\n\nOn this blog, I plan to write about:\n\n- \ud83d\udda5\ufe0f **Homelab adventures** \u2014 documenting my self-hosting journey, from Proxmox setups to Docker deployments\n- \ud83c\udf10 **Networking** \u2014 tips and tricks on VPN configurations, firewall rules, and network automation\n- \ud83d\udcbb **Backend development** \u2014 things I learn while working with Go, PHP, and databases\n- \ud83e\udd16 **Automation** \u2014 scripts, tools, and workflows that make life easier\n- \ud83d\udcdd **General tech musings** \u2014 thoughts on the tech world and things I find interesting\n\n## Why Blog?\n\nI believe in learning in public. Writing things down not only helps me solidify my understanding, but also (hopefully) helps others who are on a similar journey. Plus, it's a great way to look back and see how much I've grown.\n\n## Stay Tuned\n\nThis is just the beginning. I have a lot of topics I'm excited to explore and share. If any of the topics above interest you, stick around \u2014 there's plenty more to come!\n\nThanks for reading, and welcome to my corner of the internet. \ud83d\ude80",
